			  "Agents": {
			    "Internal": {
			      "Version": "1.1.0"
			    }
			  },
			  "CustomInstructions": "“% Calls Answered in Primary” corresponds to 'Data'[% New New is 1]\nThis represents the percentage of calls answered in primary, meaning the call was answered by a nurse primarily responsible for client.\n\n“% Under 60 Seconds” corresponds to 'Data'[Pct_Under60]\nThis represents the percentage of calls answered in under 60 seconds.\n\n“Call Volume” corresponds to 'Data'[Row Count]\nThis represents the total number of calls received during the selected time period.\n\n“Average Wait Time” corresponds to 'Data'[AVG Wait Time]\nThis represents the average wait time in minutes a caller experiences before a nurse answers.  Please multiple by 60 to convert to seconds for responses as applicable.\n\n“Average Talk Time” corresponds to 'Data'[Avg Talk Time]\nThis represents the average length of time in seconds nurses spend on the call with the patient or caregiver.  Please divide by 60 to convert to minutes for responses as applicable.\n\nAll metrics must filter 'Data'[Call Result] = ‘Answered’ unless the user explicitly says otherwise.\n\n\"Nurse\" corresponds to 'Data'[Contact Agent Name]\nThis represents the nurse taking the call.\n\n\"Team\" corresponds to 'Data'[Team]\nThis is the Team responsible for this call based on a reference table which indicates which Team is responsible during a given hour during a given day of the week\n\n\"Queue\" corresponds to 'Data'[Contact Skill Name]\nThis is the call queue which ultimately routed the call.\n\nDate references refer to 'Data'[Reporting Date]\n\nWhen asking for lowest values of some kind (e.g. - lowest average talk times per nurse) disregard anything that averages to be blank, null, or 0.\n\n\"Rollover Queue\" corresponds to 'Data'[Contains ROQ?] when this is a \"Y\" it means that the call was sent to Rollover Queue.  When it's an \"N\" it's not sent to rollover queue.\n\n'Data'[Wait Seconds] is row-level wait time in seconds which is the underlying per-call wait times or per‑call wait time column in the data\n\n'Data'[Talk Seconds] is row-level talk time in seconds which is the underlying per-call talk times or per‑call talk time column in the data."
			}
		contentType: json

